# Retainer — root environment.
#
# Copy to `.env` and edit. `.env` is gitignored; `.env.example` is the only env file
# that is ever committed. Real credentials live in ~/.config/retainer/, never in the tree.
#
# This is a yarn-workspaces monorepo and MOST configuration is per package, not here:
#
#   packages/hardhat/.env    contracts: RPC, deployer key, deploy-time terms
#   packages/nextjs/.env     resource server + browser: x402, pricing, seller key
#
# Each has its own .env.example. Start with those two — the app needs nothing from this
# file to run. What lives here is only what runs from the repo root: the end-to-end tests.

# --- End-to-end tests (Playwright, run from the root: `yarn e2e`) ---

# Port Playwright starts the app on, and the base URL the specs assume.
# Both have working defaults; set them only if 3000 is taken.
# E2E_PORT=3000
# E2E_BASE_URL=http://localhost:3000

# Optional. Point the gate spec at a DEPLOYED service instead of a local build, to check
# that the live x402 gate still answers 402 before its access window opens. The live-gate
# test SKIPS when this is unset, which is why CI can run the suite without a deployment.
#   E2E_LIVE_BASE_URL=https://retainer.edycu.dev yarn e2e
# E2E_LIVE_BASE_URL=

# --- Not used by this project ---
#
# A local `.env` inherited from the scaffold template may still define MINIO_ROOT_USER,
# MINIO_ROOT_PASSWORD and S3_BUCKET. They belonged to a self-hosted x402 facilitator that
# this project does not run: settlement goes through the hosted Blocky402 testnet
# facilitator, which the Hedera bounty requires and which needs no account or API key.
# Nothing in this repository reads those three variables. They are deliberately absent here
# rather than copied forward, so this file cannot send anyone configuring credentials that
# do nothing.
